---
import PageHero from "@/components/PageHero.astro";
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const title = "Privacy Policy";
const description =
  "How the Kingsport Amateur Radio Club (W4TRC) collects, uses, and protects information on w4trc.org, our forms, and the membership site.";
const updated = "November 23, 2026";
---

<Base title={title} meta_title="KARC - Privacy Policy" description={description}>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Policy"
    title={title}
    subtitle={`Last updated ${updated}`}
  />

  <section class="section-md">
    <div class="max-w-[900px] mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="prose max-w-none content">
        <p>
          The Kingsport Amateur Radio Club ("KARC", "the club", "we") runs w4trc.org and the related
          sites listed below. This policy explains what information we collect, why, and the choices
          you have. Questions or requests go to
          <a href="mailto:contact@w4trc.org">contact@w4trc.org</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What this policy covers</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>w4trc.org</strong>, the club's main website</li>
          <li><strong>members.w4trc.org</strong>, where members join, renew, and pay dues, and where anyone can donate</li>
          <li><strong>forms.w4trc.org</strong>, for event RSVPs, surveys, and board feedback</li>
          <li>Other club subdomains, such as the photo gallery and repeater status pages</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Information you give us</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Contact form.</strong> Your name, email address, and message. The form is sent
            straight to the club's email (contact@w4trc.org) using Cloudflare, which already hosts this
            site. We do not store form submissions on the website.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Membership and dues.</strong> Your name, callsign, email, phone number, mailing
            address, membership type, and payment history. We use this to keep the membership roster,
            track dues, and contact members about club business.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Payments and donations.</strong> Online payments are handled by
            <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Stripe</a>. Your card details go directly
            to Stripe. The club does not see or store your full card number.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Event RSVPs and surveys.</strong> Whatever you enter, usually your name, callsign,
            and email. The anonymous board feedback form does not ask for your name.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Photos you upload.</strong> Photos sent through our upload link may appear in the
            gallery, on this website, or in the Zero-Beat newsletter.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Advertising.</strong> We run Google Search ads to help people find the club. Our site
            uses the Google Ads tag, which sets cookies so Google can tell us when someone who clicked an
            ad goes on to visit pages or take actions such as joining. Google may use this information as
            described in
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Site analytics.</strong> We use <a href="https://www.rybbit.io/" rel="noopener">Rybbit</a>,
            a privacy-focused analytics tool, to count visits and see which pages are popular. It does not
            use cookies to track you across other websites.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Embedded content.</strong> Some pages load content from other services. These include
            fonts from Google Fonts, the weather widget (weatherwidget.io), solar conditions (hamqsl.com),
            and YouTube videos. Those services receive your IP address and may set their own cookies.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Announcement banner.</strong> If you close the banner at the top of the site, we set a
            small cookie so it stays closed for a few days.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How we use information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To answer your messages and run club membership, dues, and events</li>
          <li>To send club news and meeting information to members</li>
          <li>To understand how the website is used and improve it</li>
          <li>To measure whether our ads are working</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>We do not sell your personal information.</strong> We share it only with the services
          named above that help us run the club, or when required by law.
        </p>

        <h2>Public amateur radio information</h2>
        <p>
          Amateur radio callsigns and license details are public records published by the FCC. The club
          may publish members' names and callsigns on this site, for example in officer listings, meeting
          minutes, event recaps, member articles, and Silent Key memorials. If you would like something
          about you changed or removed, email us.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Ad personalization:</strong> manage or turn off personalized Google ads at
            <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener">My Ad Center</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Cookies:</strong> you can block or delete cookies in your browser settings. The site
            still works without them.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Your records:</strong> email
            <a href="mailto:contact@w4trc.org">contact@w4trc.org</a> to see, correct, or delete the
            information the club holds about you. We may need to keep some records, such as dues and
            donation history, for the club's financial records.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Keeping information safe</h2>
        <p>
          Access to membership records is limited to club officers who need it for club business. No
          system is perfectly secure, but we take reasonable steps to protect the information you give us.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          Young people are welcome in amateur radio, but this website is not directed at children under
          13, and we do not knowingly collect their personal information online. A parent or guardian
          should handle membership for a minor.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy as the club's sites and services change. The date at the top of this
          page shows when it was last updated.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
